  "description": "News ledes for the new core's stories, keyed by the event kind they report (a closure, a death, a filing, a law taking effect, an election result, a council vote, a budget). News sources give patterns only; every part here is a whole sentence said in public-domain federal records (the Congressional Record, hearings, federal oral histories), with record words as slots.",
  "slots": {
    "subject": "The business or office that closed, from the event record.",
    "name": "A person, by name, from the records.",
    "place": "A place, from the place records.",
    "year": "A year from the event's date.",
    "date": "A date from the event record, as people say it.",
    "number": "A count from the event record.",
    "age": "An age, computed from the birth record.",
    "pronoun": "His, her or their, from the person's record.",
    "pronoun_sub": "He, she or they, from the person's record.",
    "office": "The office, from the contest record.",
    "wage": "An hourly wage, from the law record.",
    "opponent": "The other candidate, from the contest record.",
    "percent": "A vote share, from the results record.",
    "count": "A vote count such as 5 to 2, from the vote record.",
    "measure": "The measure, as its record names it.",
    "action": "What the body voted to do, from the measure record.",
    "money": "A dollar amount, from the budget record.",
    "purpose": "What the money is for, from the budget record."
  },
